  m_Name: Occipital_Lobe
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ModelPartDataSO
  id: Occipital_Lobe
  partName: Occipital Lobe
  descriptionChunks:
  - The occipital lobe is responsible for processing visual information received
    from the eyes. It interprets signals related to color, shape, and movement, allowing
    the organism to understand and interact with its surroundings.
  - This region is essential for visual perception and spatial awareness. By converting
    sensory input into meaningful images, it supports navigation and environmental
    interaction. Proper function of the occipital lobe is critical for recognizing
    objects and responding appropriately to visual stimuli.
